<section class="band why" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-h">
  <div class="wrap why-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Why work with me</p>
      <h2 class="h-sec" id="why-h">Advice is easy to find. Experience is harder to buy.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="why-copy">
      <p>I have spent much of my career on the other side of the table: building businesses, managing people, winning and losing customers, investing in new ideas, and making decisions when there isn't an obvious answer.</p>
      <p>I understand what it is like to carry responsibility for a business. And I know that the right strategy means very little unless someone can make it work.</p>
      <p>I bring that experience to the leaders I advise: independent thinking, commercial perspective and a willingness to get involved.</p>
      <ul class="why-facts">
        <li>Founded Digital Clarity in 2002 and grew it to more than 200 clients</li>
        <li>Built DC Storm through to its acquisition by Rakuten</li>
        <li>Led commercial operations for an internet business listed in Singapore</li>
        <li>COO and Executive Director of a US public company since 2011</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band" id="story" aria-labelledby="story-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chap-head">
      <h2 class="h-sec" id="story-h">Experience</h2>
      <p>Twenty-five years on the operating side: building a business, taking a product to exit, leading commercial teams and carrying executive responsibility in a US public company.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="chapters">
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">01</span>
        <h3><span class="when">Earlier career</span>VNU and Ziff Davis</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>Technology publishing and advertising sales roles across Europe. A grounding in technology markets, enterprise customers and commercial growth.</p></div>
              </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">02</span>
        <h3><span class="when">Before 2002</span>AltaVista and Singapore</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>AltaVista's global sales team in the formative years of internet search, working with HP and Compaq. Then led commercial operations at a Singapore internet business that listed on SIMEX and was acquired by an Indian technology company.</p><span class="tag">Listed, then acquired</span></div>
        <img class="pic" src="/assets/img/trails-vertical.webp" width="900" height="1600" alt="Light trails from traffic passing a lit building at night" loading="lazy">
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">03</span>
        <h3><span class="when">2002</span>Digital Clarity</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>Founded the business and built it to 25 to 30 people working with more than 200 clients. Evolved the offer from search and performance marketing into strategic growth and go-to-market advisory.</p><span class="tag">Founder</span></div>
        <img class="pic" src="/assets/img/office-night.webp" width="2000" height="1125" alt="A team working late in a lit office, seen from the street at night" loading="lazy">
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">04</span>
        <h3><span class="when">Built within Digital Clarity</span>DC Storm</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>Identified the difficulty of measuring marketing performance across fragmented digital channels and built a technology proposition to address it. Led product, positioning, sales and partnerships through to customer adoption. Around 48% of major media planning and buying agencies used the platform before its acquisition by Rakuten.</p><span class="tag amber">Acquired by Rakuten</span></div>
        <div class="pic-blank" aria-hidden="true"><b>48%</b><span>of major media agencies on the platform at exit</span></div>
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">05</span>
        <h3><span class="when">2011</span>DBMM Group</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>COO, Senior Vice President and Executive Director of Digital Brand Media &amp; Marketing Group, Inc., quoted in the US as OTC: DBMM, with Digital Clarity as its wholly owned operating business.</p><span class="tag">US public company</span></div>
        <img class="pic" src="/assets/img/tower.webp" width="1600" height="1066" alt="An office building at night with every floor lit" loading="lazy">
      </li>
      <li class="chapter">
        <span class="n">06</span>
        <h3><span class="when">Today</span>Advisory</h3>
        <div class="body"><p>Advising CEOs, founders, boards and investors on growth, investment and direction, and working hands-on where that helps.</p><span class="tag">Advisory</span></div>
